@@ -36,9 +36,10 @@ People are `members/{lowercase email}`: `{name, email, role: "admin"|"member", a
 |---|---|
 | `docs/index.html` | Home: tool tiles for what the viewer can use; Team tile for admins. |
 | `docs/assets/core.js` | Shared by every page: Firebase init, sign-in screen (Google + email/password + reset), member lookup, access levels (`APP.level(tool)`), top bar, `window.claude` adapter. Tool list `TOOLS` lives here (set `ready:true` when a tool ships). Demo mode on localhost. |
-| `docs/assets/core.css` | Shared tokens (light/dark), top bar, sign-in card, tiles, buttons. |
+| `docs/assets/core.css` | Shared tokens (light/dark), top bar, sign-in card, tiles, buttons. Brand: white background, accent = the AP logo's lavender (`#8482a7`, deepened to `#625f8f` for buttons). |
+| `docs/assets/logo.png`, `favicon.png`, `apple-touch-icon.png` | Aurora Promotions AP logo (top bar, sign-in card, browser tab and phone icon; core.js adds the icon links to every page). |
 | `docs/team/index.html` | Team & Access (admins only): add/edit people, login type, role, per-tool access, on/off, send password email. |
-| `docs/projects/index.html` | **Projects** (tool key `projects`): **internal team work only, no client or invoice links** (user, 2026-10-02). `projects/{id}`: name, status (list in `settings/projects.statuses`; "done"/"cancel" in the name = finished), priority, startDate, dueDate, lead, team[emails], description. `tasks/{id}`: projectId, title, assignee (email), dueDate, priority, status todo/doing/review/done, progress 0–100, order, team[] (copied from the project, kept in sync; rules use it), comments[{by,name,at,text}], assignedAt/By, doneAt. Optional standard tasks (`settings/projects.steps`, default empty). Full = everything; limited = projects/tasks whose team includes them, add tasks for themselves, edit own tasks (no reassign), comment (only `comments`+`updatedAt` change), no delete. Views: My tasks, Board (drag & drop), Projects, Settings (full). `?project=<id>` opens one. |
+| `docs/projects/index.html` | **Projects** (tool key `projects`): **internal team work only, no client or invoice links** (user, 2026-10-02). `projects/{id}`: name, status (list in `settings/projects.statuses`; "done"/"cancel" in the name = finished), priority, startDate, dueDate, lead, team[emails], description. `tasks/{id}`: projectId, title, assignee (email), dueDate, priority, status todo/doing/review/blocked/done, progress 0–100, order, team[] (copied from the project, kept in sync; rules use it), comments[{by,name,at,text}], assignedAt/By, doneAt. Optional standard tasks (`settings/projects.steps`, default empty). Full = everything; limited = projects/tasks whose team includes them, add tasks for themselves, edit own tasks (no reassign), comment (only `comments`+`updatedAt` change), no delete. Views: Overview (team dashboard: KPIs, team progress per person, deadlines, project progress, tasks by status, latest updates derived from tasks/comments, star of the week), My tasks (cards with autosaving progress slider, status, ✓ Done, Add note), Board (5 columns, drag & drop), Projects (cards; progress = average task progress), Team (people, workload, person drawer), Settings (full). Moving progress above 0 on a To do task sets In progress; Done sets 100% and shows confetti. `?project=<id>` opens one. |
 | `docs/clients/index.html` | **Clients & Seasons** (tool key `clients`). `clients/{key}` = a contact person (key = lowercase email, else `nc--<name>--<company>` slug): name, company, email, phone, title, owner (rep **name**, = salesRep on their first order; full users can reassign), ownerSource, tags[], notes, dnc. Full users auto-create missing client docs from orders on page load; limited users see "virtual" clients from their own orders until they act on one. Stats (invoices, sales before tax excl. quote/cancelled statuses, first/last order, months) are computed live from visible orders. `seasons/{id}`: type (from `settings/clients.types`), year, name, outreachStart/End, catalogUrl, products, subject, body (fill-ins {first_name} {name} {company} {season} {catalog_link} {products} {rep_name}), target {mode: all/buyers/lastyear/tags/manual, tags[]}. `outreach/{seasonId__clientId}`: owner, status todo/sent/replied/quote/ordered/not_interested/no_reply/stopped/skipped, sentAt, followups, nextFollowUp (= today + `followupDays`, default 4; after `maxFollowups`, default 2, → no_reply), history[]. "Due" = sent and nextFollowUp ≤ today. Emails open as Gmail (`authuser`=member email) / Outlook web / mailto compose links; choice kept in localStorage `cs-send`. Rules: limited = owner == their name, no delete; seasons and settings full only. |
 | `docs/assets/gmail.js` | Gmail sending for Clients & Seasons, entirely in the browser: Google Identity Services token client (scopes `gmail.send` + `gmail.metadata`, `login_hint` = member email) and Gmail REST (`messages.send` with threadId/In-Reply-To for follow-ups; `threads.get` metadata to detect replies = any message without the SENT label). Token kept in sessionStorage (~1 h). Available only for `@aurorapromotions.ca` members and when `GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` is set in `docs/firebase-config.js` (OAuth consent screen must be **Internal**; authorized JS origins = the dashboard address + `http://localhost:8093`). Simulated in demo mode. **Hard rule from the user (2026-10-02): no email may reach a client without the approval of that client's own sales rep.** So: only the owner rep sees send controls (two-click Approve & send, second click shows the recipient); full users can only save `outreach.draft` for the rep; nothing is ever sent automatically (follow-ups too need approval). Never add auto-send, scheduled send or send-on-behalf. |
 | `docs/acceptance/` | **Order Acceptance** (tool key `acceptance`). `index.html`: Terms & Conditions viewer (print/PDF), editor (full only) and version history. `terms/v{n}` = {version, effectiveDate, company{name,address,email,phone,website,province}, sections[{title,body}], note, createdAt/By/ByName}; rules: read with any acceptance access, create by full, **never update/delete** (immutable so acceptances can cite a version). `terms-default.js` = starting draft (Ontario; shipping, damage claims, force majeure incl. carrier/port/border strikes, customs, tariffs, supplier shutdowns; cancellations: full refund only before production; 2%/month = 26.82%/yr; not legal advice). `{company}`/`{province}` placeholders. Client acceptance: `acceptances/{28-char random token}` = snapshot {invoiceNumber, salesRep, client*, deliveryAddress, inHandsDate, orderDate, lines[{product,details,qty,unitPrice,amount}], subtotal, tax (line customerTaxPct or settings default), total, terms{version,effectiveDate,company,sections}, payment{provider stripe/square, url}, message, status draft→sent→accepted→paid / cancelled, history[], acceptedName/acceptedAt(server time)/acceptedUserAgent, paidAt}. Public page `docs/accept/index.html` (no core.js, no sign-in) reads it with `get` and the client may only flip sent→accepted with name + `request.time`. Staff cannot set "accepted" or touch accepted* fields; after acceptance only status/payment/paid/history change; accepted ones can never be deleted. Only the invoice's rep sends (Gmail two-click). Mark as paid also sets orders.invoicePaidDate. Sales By-order "Acceptance" column links here (`acceptance/?invoice=` / `?id=`). Stripe/Square are payment links pasted by the rep; automatic paid status would need a server with their secret keys. |
