index 633f8c1..689ca8a 100644
--- a/docs/handbook/index.html
+++ b/docs/handbook/index.html
@@ -158,8 +158,9 @@ Net profit       = Gross profit − Rep commission ($) − Platform fee − Cust
 <ul>
   <li><b>Project:</b> name, status (editable list in Projects → Settings; a status containing "Done" or "Cancel" counts as finished), priority, start and due dates, a <b>project lead</b>, the <b>team</b>, and notes.</li>
   <li><b>Standard tasks</b> (optional): a list in Projects → Settings that can be added to a new project in one click, assigned to the lead.</li>
-  <li><b>Task:</b> title, assigned person, due date, priority, status (<i>To do → In progress → Review → Done</i>), progress %, details and comments. Marking a task Done sets progress to 100%. A task is <b>late</b> when its due date has passed and it isn't done.</li>
-  <li><b>Views:</b> <i>My tasks</i> (your tasks grouped into Late / This week / Later / No date, with a "New" mark on tasks assigned since your last visit), <i>Board</i> (drag cards between status columns), <i>Projects</i> (progress bar = done tasks ÷ all tasks).</li>
+  <li><b>Task:</b> title, assigned person, due date, priority, status (<i>To do → In progress → Review → Done</i>, or <i>Blocked</i> when someone is stuck), progress %, details and comments. Marking a task Done sets progress to 100% (with a small confetti celebration); moving a To do task's progress above 0% moves it to In progress. A task is <b>late</b> when its due date has passed and it isn't done.</li>
+  <li><b>Views:</b> <i>Overview</i> (team dashboard: open / in progress / late / done this week, team progress per person, deadlines for the next 7 days, project progress, tasks by status, latest updates and a "star of the week" = most tasks finished in 7 days), <i>My tasks</i> (your tasks grouped into Needs attention (late or blocked) / In progress / To do / In review / Done, each with a progress slider that saves by itself, a status menu, a <b>✓ Done</b> button and <b>Add note</b>; a "New" mark on tasks assigned since your last visit), <i>Board</i> (drag cards between the five status columns), <i>Projects</i> (cards; progress = average progress of the project's tasks), <i>Team</i> (each person's open tasks, average progress, late tasks and workload: Available / Light / Balanced / Heavy; click a person for their tasks and updates).</li>
+  <li><b>Latest updates</b> are worked out from the tasks themselves (created, assigned, finished, comments); nothing extra is stored.</li>
 </ul>
 <table><thead><tr><th>Access</th><th>In Projects they can…</th></tr></thead><tbody>
 <tr><td><b>Full</b> (admins, team leads)</td><td>See every project; create, edit and delete projects and tasks; assign anyone (assigning someone outside the team adds them to it); change Projects settings.</td></tr>
@@ -326,6 +327,7 @@ Net profit       = Gross profit − Rep commission ($) − Platform fee − Cust
   <li><b>2 Oct 2026:</b> Tools connected (home Today cards, invoice ↔ project ↔ client links, season sales). Order Acceptance started with versioned Terms &amp; Conditions including shipping and force majeure.</li>
   <li><b>2 Oct 2026:</b> Client acceptance: private accept page with order summary + terms, Stripe or Square payment links, rep-approved sending, Mark as paid.</li>
   <li><b>2 Oct 2026:</b> Projects changed to internal team work only (no client or invoice links), as requested.</li>
+  <li><b>5 Oct 2026:</b> Projects upgraded with the Aurora team tracker features: Overview dashboard, My tasks with progress sliders and a Done button, Blocked status, Team view with workload, project cards. Same data and security rules as before. Aurora Promotions branding: AP logo in the top bar, sign-in and browser tab; white background with the logo's lavender as the accent colour.</li>
 </ul>
